==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|qindarka|s}}

# {{qual|plural: qindarka or qintars}} An [[Albanian]] [[coin]] equal to one [[hundredth]] of a [[lek]].
# {{qual|plural: qintars}} A unit of measure, which varies in value depending upon the product measured; for example, a qintar of cotton might be 160 [[kg]] of cotton, 50 kg of cotton lint; a qintar of lime, 65 kg.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2002|author=Jonathan M. Bloom|author2=Sheila S. Blair|title=Islam: A Thousand Years of Faith and Power
|passage=For all its squalor '''''qintars''''' and '''''qintars''''' of gold dust are traded there.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=Muhammad Khalid Masud|author2=Rudolph Peters|author3=David Stephan Powers|title=Dispensing Justice in Islam: Qadis and their judgments
|passage={{...}} who offered 190 piasters per year for rent, 20 piasters more than the other, plus half a '''qintar''' of pomegranates.}}

